RISC OS: keep the icon bar from popping up over full screen.

With the icon bar's "bring to front automatically" option, it came forward
over the full screen game whenever the pointer reached the bottom of the
screen. As riscos-mesa 20.3.5-17's SDL and freeglut back ends do: while the
pointer is over the full screen window, the mouse's bounding box
(OS_Word 21,1) stops a few pixels above the bottom, and the lowest row the
pointer can reach counts as the bottom row, so the game still sees the
pointer reach the bottom edge. The whole screen comes back when the pointer
is over anything else, out of full screen, when the window closes and at
exit; after a mode change (the OS resets the box) it's set again.
YSFlight$PointerMargin sets the margin in screen pixels (default 2, 0 = off).
Host test: tests/host-window.

